{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"The `search` deployment couldn't create pods, and it's now running again. I submitted the mitigation. I didn't wait for the validation result, and I didn't send any test requests to confirm that end-user requests succeed.\n\nThe namespace has a `memory-limit-quota` ResourceQuota (1Gi). It rejects any pod that doesn't set a memory request or limit. The `search` container had CPU settings only, so its ReplicaSet kept failing with \"must specify memory\". I added a 128Mi memory request and a 256Mi limit with `kubectl set resources deploy/search`. The new pod started, registered with consul, and the old ReplicaSet scaled down.\n\nThe other deployments, such as `geo`, also have no memory settings. They're running because they were created before the quota applied. If any of them restarts, it will probably hit the same error."}}
